### Session 194-INFRA — 2026-07-29 — **56% OF THE CORPUS HAD BEEN RENDERING IN TIMES NEW ROMAN, AND THE INTEGRITY GATE HAD BEEN REPORTING ON 6 OF ITS 11 CHECKS** — two defects the site's entire body of law was structurally incapable of seeing, because 21,000 words of standards contained the word "font" zero times

**No prose was edited. No argument was touched.** Infrastructure only, run against the deployed corpus. Full forensic record: `archive/S194-forensic-audit-and-fix-order.md`.

**Shipped** — `validate-site.js`: the verdict banner moved to the END of the file (it printed `ALL CHECKS PASSED` after CHECK 6, *before* CHECKS 7–11 ran; every session for months closed on a green light that had seen 6 of 11 checks) · **CHECK 12** critical-path payload · **CHECK 13** web-font delivery + undefined CSS custom properties · **CHECK 14** the article-tag literal contract · `global.css` gained `--font-heading/-body/-mono` in `:root` (referenced 127×, defined nowhere) and lost 13 obsolete v2 mega-menu rules · 4 new idempotent repair scripts (`fix-script-payload`, `fix-missing-webfonts`, `fix-skip-links`, `strip-stale-nav-comment`) · CLAUDE.md gained **PRESENTATION INTEGRITY** and **THE LITERAL-STRING TRAP**.

**Fixed** — **361 pages restored to Playfair Display + Inter** (`global.css` demanded both, supplied neither; the only source was a Google Fonts `<link>` present on 325 of 687 pages — 347 live articles rendered in Times New Roman + Arial, and **340 of the broken pages carried a `preconnect` to a font host they never requested**, the fingerprint of an automated performance pass optimising the loading of nothing) · **127 CSS declarations un-dropped** (an undefined custom property is invalid at computed-value time and `font-family` inherits, so `var(--font-heading)` silently took the *parent's* font rather than falling through to the `h1-h4` rule; 28 live rules affected) · **all JS off the critical path** site-wide (`nav.js` 184 KB — 81% of it a static menu blob — was render-blocking on all 687 pages; homepage blocking payload ~1,000 KB → 348 KB, now entirely CSS) · **skip-to-content 115 → 660** working links · 79 KB of stale pasted nav-template comment stripped from 86 pages · repo 2.9 GB → 1.3 GB via `git gc` (Aaron ran it).

**Surprise, and the one to carry forward** — **11 pages had shipped with `id`-before-`class` on the article tag and were invisible to all 21 scripts that match that literal, since the day they were written.** Never counted, never audited, never linted. Normalising them surfaced 85 pre-existing inline-style attributes, so **CHECK 10 re-baselined 224/639 → 235/724 — this was discovered debt, not the ratchet loosening**, and the reason is annotated in the code. A skip-link pass in this session briefly reproduced the same fault at scale (560 of 618 pages dark) **while the validator still reported every check passing**, because CHECK 11 does `if (open === -1) continue`. CHECK 14 now holds the contract; the real repayment is still owed — sweep those 21 scripts to a tolerant regex.

**Method note** — three findings this session were initially wrong because a `grep` hit was read without checking its usage: a commented-out `<script>` counted as a live duplicate (41 phantom "double-loads"), a comment-header mention of the article literal read as a runtime dependency in `share-bar.js` (it uses `querySelector`, and was never affected), and `/<!--[^]*?MARKER[^]*?-->/` anchoring on the earliest `<!--` in the file and swallowing a `global.css` link on 10 pages. All caught and corrected in-session. **Grep locates; it does not establish.**

**Carries forward** — the `global.css` critical-CSS split (348 KB blocking, now the entire critical path) is the big remaining infrastructure job and was **deliberately not attempted on a low compute budget**: its failure mode is all 687 pages rendering broken with no visual regression test in the repo. Do not bulk-prune — a conservative pass found only 36 KB confidently dead across ~150 scattered families. Brief is in `archive/NEXT-SESSION-S195-kickoff.md`.

**Pipeline** — all seven scripts + validator: **ALL 14 CHECKS PASSED**, canonical 611 unchanged, 618 pages visible to the literal matchers, 686/686 supplying their typefaces. Deploy verified live (`global.css` served with the new `:root` tokens). Deviation from baseline: validator is now 14 checks, not 11.

